---
// Privacy policy for Meta (Facebook and Instagram) and LinkedIn lead ads.
// Deliberately NOT linked from the nav, footer or any other page, and excluded
// from the sitemap and search indexing. The URL is given only inside the ad
// platforms' lead form settings, where a privacy policy link is mandatory.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, contact } from '../lib/config';

const updated = '3 September 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How City Property Services collects, uses and protects the personal information of people who enquire with us."
  noindex
>
  <main class="wrap legal">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="h1" style="margin-top:12px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="body-lg muted" style="max-width:62ch;margin-top:16px;">
        This policy explains what personal information {site.name} collects, why we collect it,
        how we use and protect it, and the choices you have. Last updated {updated}.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is a real estate consultancy based in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, India. We help people
        and businesses buy, sell, rent, lease and invest in residential, commercial, industrial and
        land assets. In this policy, "we", "us" and "our" mean {site.name}.
      </p>
      <p class="contact-block">
        {contact.address}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a><br />
        Phone: {contact.phone}<br />
        RERA registration: {site.rera}
      </p>

      <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to personal information we collect through our website at {site.url},
        through enquiry forms on our website, through lead forms you submit on Meta platforms
        (Facebook and Instagram) and on LinkedIn, and through phone, WhatsApp and email
        conversations with our team.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p><strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you submit an enquiry, we typically collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your phone number and WhatsApp number</li>
        <li>Your email address</li>
        <li>Your city or preferred locality</li>
        <li>Your requirement, such as property type, budget, size and timeline</li>
        <li>Any message or details you choose to share with us</li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>Information from advertising platforms.</strong> If you respond to one of our
        advertisements on Facebook, Instagram or LinkedIn and submit an instant lead form on that
        platform, the platform passes the details you submitted in that form to us. We receive only
        the fields shown in the form at the time you submitted it. We do not receive your password,
        your friends or connections list, or any part of your profile you did not choose to share.</p>

      <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> When you visit our website we may
        collect standard technical information such as your browser and device type, approximate
        location derived from your IP address, the pages you viewed, and how you arrived at the site.
        This is collected through cookies and similar technologies.</p>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry and contact you about it</li>
        <li>To understand your requirement and share suitable property options</li>
        <li>To arrange site visits, viewings and meetings</li>
        <li>To provide advisory, transaction and documentation support</li>
        <li>To send you relevant property updates and offers, where you have agreed to receive them</li>
        <li>To improve our website, our services and our advertising</li>
        <li>To keep records and to comply with legal and regulatory obligations</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We contact enquirers by phone, WhatsApp, SMS and email. You can ask us to stop at any time
        and we will honour that request.
      </p>

      <h2>Our basis for processing</h2>
      <p>
        We process your personal information with your consent, given when you submit an enquiry or a
        lead form, and where processing is necessary to provide the service you asked for or to meet a
        legal obligation. Where Indian law applies, we handle personal data in line with the Digital
        Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the rules made under it. You may withdraw your consent
        at any time using the contact details in this policy.
      </p>

      <h2>How we share information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only as described below:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Developers, owners, sellers and landlords</strong>, where sharing your name and
          contact details is necessary to progress the specific enquiry you made with us, for example
          to register you for a site visit or to make an offer on your behalf</li>
        <li><strong>Service providers</strong> who help us run our business, such as website hosting,
          form and email delivery, analytics and customer records providers. They may process your
          information only on our instructions</li>
        <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> such as lawyers and accountants where required</li>
        <li><strong>Authorities</strong> where we are required to disclose information by law, court
          order or a valid regulatory request</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Advertising on Meta and LinkedIn</h2>
      <p>
        We advertise on Facebook and Instagram, which are operated by Meta, and on LinkedIn. When you
        submit a lead form on those platforms, the platform collects your details under its own privacy
        policy and then shares them with us. Once we receive them, this policy governs how we use them.
        We may also use these platforms' advertising tools to show ads to people who have visited our
        website or who resemble our existing audience. We do not receive information that identifies
        you personally from those advertising tools beyond what you submit to us directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can review the platforms' own policies and controls at
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Meta Privacy Policy</a>
        and
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">LinkedIn Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Our website uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site, for example which
        pages are viewed and how people found us. This helps us improve the site. Analytics data is
        collected in aggregate and we do not use it to identify you personally. You can block or delete
        cookies in your browser settings, and you can opt out of Google Analytics using the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Analytics opt out browser add on</a>.
        Blocking cookies may affect how parts of the site work.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep your information</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiry information for as long as needed to serve your requirement and to maintain
        our business records, and for as long as required by applicable law. Property transactions can
        take time and buyers often return later, so we may retain your details for a reasonable period
        after your last contact with us. You can ask us to delete your information sooner.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable law, you may ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Confirm what personal information we hold about you and give you a copy</li>
        <li>Correct information that is inaccurate, incomplete or out of date</li>
        <li>Delete your personal information where we no longer need it</li>
        <li>Stop sending you marketing messages, calls or WhatsApp updates</li>
        <li>Withdraw a consent you previously gave us</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To make any of these requests, email us at
        <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or call {contact.phone}. We may need to
        verify your identity before we act. We aim to respond within a reasonable time and in any case
        within the period required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information against
        loss, misuse and unauthorised access or disclosure. Our website is served over an encrypted
        HTTPS connection. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot
        guarantee absolute security, but we work to protect your information and to limit access to the
        people who need it.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
        anyone under the age of 18. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information,
        contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Our website and our advertisements may link to third party websites, including developer and
        project websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites.
        Please read their privacy policies before sharing your information with them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or in the law.
        The date at the top of this page shows when it was last updated. Please review it periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact and grievances</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a question, a request or a complaint about how we handle your personal information,
        please contact us. We take concerns seriously and will work with you to resolve them.
      </p>
      <p class="contact-block">
        {site.name}<br />
        {contact.address}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a><br />
        Phone: {contact.phone}
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 820px; }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .legal h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal p { margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text); }
  .legal ul { margin: 0 0 18px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text); }
  .legal a { color: var(--navy); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal a:hover { opacity: .8; }
  .legal .contact-block {
    background: var(--surface-2, #f4f6f8);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm, 8px);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .legal .section { padding-block: 8px 72px; }
</style>
